<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Marieberg seeks Duni part owner.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Marieberg seeks Duni part owner.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish publishing concern Tidnings AB Marieberg said on Thursday it was in discussions to bring in a part-owner for its wholly-owned disposable tableware unit Duni.</p>
<p>Marieberg said in a statement it aimed to boost financing for Duni's future growth. It said Duni currently had an annual turnover of five billion crowns with sales on average doubling every five years.</p>
<p>Marieberg rose 2.50 crowns to 153 after the news.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
